# Secure Boot with keys the machine generates and owns.
#
# sbctl is the whole addon: an 11 MiB static Go binary, no daemon, no listening
# socket, no privileged path. It is what limine-entry-tool and mkinitcpio
# already look for when they decide whether to sign what they just wrote, so
# installing it (and creating keys) is what turns the existing boot pipeline
# into a signing one. Doing the same with sbsign from sbsigntools would mean
# writing and maintaining three hooks to replace code that already ships.
#
# Not in the core: a machine whose firmware cannot or will not enforce Secure
# Boot carries no signing tool.
sbctl
